dialogue trust_cleric_3
title: The book of names
trigger: Trust cleric level=3
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  Rain on the wagon cover. The Cleric sits under it with a lamp turned low and a small book open on one knee, its pages soft and swollen from fen damp.
  -> book

node book hero
  I said I'd show you the book. Sit, if you like. It isn't long. It only feels long.
  -> names

node names hero
  Every name in here is someone I steadied at the tithe tables who came back Hollow anyway. I write them down so somebody does. The Choir doesn't. To the Choir they're a sum that came out right.
  -> last

node last hero
  The last one is a hold girl, maybe twelve. Her first tithe. I held her hand and told her it wouldn't hurt, and it didn't, and that was the worst of it. She just went quiet. I wrote her down that night and walked into the fen the next morning.
  -> answer

node answer commander
  The Cleric's thumb rests on the last line, over the name.
  * Read me one. Any one. -> read
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag cleric:ledger_read
  * You didn't take them. The Choir did. -> absolved
    do: AddTrust $with 5
    do: SetFlag cleric:ledger_absolved
  * You can't mend what's done. Put it away before it costs you in a fight. -> shut
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag cleric:ledger_shut
  * So that's what drove you out. Her. -> why
    if: FlagSet cleric:white_asked
    do: AddTrust $with 7
    do: SetFlag cleric:ledger_why

node read hero
  One. All right. Corran Hale, a thatcher, very bad at jokes, laughed at every one of them anyway. There. He was a person, for a breath, out loud.
  -> mend

node absolved hero
  The Choir held the cup. I held the hand. I've never been able to decide which is worse, and I've had a long time to try.
  -> mend

node shut hero
  You may be right. But a healer who forgets is just a collector with kinder hands. I'll keep it out of the fighting. I won't put it away.
  -> mend

node why hero
  You remembered I said both. Yes. Her. A hundred names before her, and it was the quiet one that did it.
  -> mend

node mend hero
  You're from before, Commander. When Halcyon was whole. Tell me. Could anyone mend the Hollow, then? Did anyone even try?
  -> truth

node truth commander
  The old memory turns the question over and finds only the edge of something, a room of white beds, and nothing more.
  * I don't remember. I won't promise you something I don't know. -> honest
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag cleric:asked_honest
  * Then we find out together, on the road. -> together
    do: AddTrust $with 4
    do: SetFlag cleric:asked_together
  * Some things can't be mended. You know that better than I do. -> hard
    do: AddTrust $with -3
    do: SetFlag cleric:asked_hard

node honest hero
  Thank you. The collectors promised everything. "It grows back." I said it too, at the tables. I'd rather have your nothing than their everything.
  -> lamp

node together hero
  Together. That's a healer's word, you know. You can't mend anyone from across a room.
  -> lamp

node hard hero
  I do. I just hoped someone from before knew better. Never mind. It was a lot to put on you.
  -> lamp

node lamp commander
  The Cleric closes the book, wraps it in oilcloth against the rain, and turns the lamp down until only the rain is left.
